till have 2s as backup for later tricks.  \n\nPassing seems too risky — landlord gets initiative at 5 cards left.  \nPlaying ♣2 is too risky with Red Joker still out.  \nPlaying ♥K is weaker than ♠A and still might be beaten by Ace or higher.  \n\n**Answer:** {"cards": ["♠A"]}  \n\n**Final output:**  \nEvaluation: Playing ♠A to force landlord to use high cards or regain control.  \nReason: We need to pressure landlord while saving 2s for later; ♠A is strong but not our highest, and could win the trick if landlord lacks immediate high cards.  \nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠A"]}'}
